@AnthropicAI · · · Oct 5, 2023 · The fact that most individual neurons are uninterpretable presents a serious roadblock to a mechanistic understanding of language models. We demonstrate a method for decomposing groups of neurons into interpretable features with the potential to move past that roadblock. 55 · 394 · 2.5K · 1.9M · Chris Olah · @ch402 · · · Mar 6, 2018 · Our most recent paper on visualizing neural networks is one of the best thing I've ever done. https://distill.pub/2018/building-blocks/… It qualitatively changes the questions we can ask. One basic example: neuron 426 fired ~= useless [floppy ear] fired = very interesting! 18 · 692 · 1.6K · Chris Olah · @ch402 · · · Sep 14, 2022 · I've never had so many "this can't possibly be true, we must have a bug" results in the course of a research project before. I'd like to take a moment to walk through some of the very strange (and surprisingly beautiful) things we found.

